A||||10||mrfixit58||Factory Sub-woofer: Replacement Speaker Options???||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-31-2000||12:17 PM||||I took my factory sub-woofer speaker down to a speaker repair store and they quoted me $50 just to install new foam around the cone.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> So, I was hoping that one of you guys have come up with a cheaper alternative. If so, were you able to match the power rating? If not cheaper, can you recommend a better speaker?<P>I want to keep the stock system. I just don't want it to rattle.<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||b lo 0||07-31-2000||12:22 PM||||If you don't mind getting sticky (not to mention woozy) you can get new foam surrounds and do it yourself for around $10-20.  Now be warned, it's a pain in the butt, but it saves you lotsa money. (I did it on 4 separate home stereo speakers-'70's era).  Look in the back of magazines like Popular Mechanics-they sell them there.  Oh, yeah, never EVER use silicone-based glue or sealant around foam surrounds-the fumes alone will eat them alive (I've seen it happen).  If you have to seal the box, you can use silicone, but don't get the speaker anywhere near it for at least 48 hours.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">  <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||07-31-2000||01:40 PM||||Don't bother fixing it yourself.. any retailer of SAS will sell you a real 6ish inch sub from their Bazooka line it will drop right in the hole with a little redrilling of the mounting holes and POOF youf got noise again! I did that sunday!!! using the factory AMP till the car is on the road.. (disassembled for painting) it was somthing to do for a couple hours. Sounds SWEET! the ported box witht the LOOONG port on the top firing into the empty dash has decent extension and the tiny factory amp doesn't sound too bad... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||b lo 0||07-31-2000||02:05 PM||||Good idea 2M6-it's nice to know people who think more logical than me live in Atlanta  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (the traffic still isn't convincing though).<BR>BTW, 2M6, we still gotta get all the Pennock's ATL-area guys together to cruise soon.  I missed Sat.'s GA Fieros meeting, but I plan on making the August meeting. See ya!||||reg||1
